# --- build output ---
server/bin/
site/dist/
site/node_modules/
spa/dist/
spa/node_modules/
mod/**/bin/
mod/**/obj/

# --- runtime data (§3: ./data/ holds events.db, projections.db, keys/, archive/) ---
#
# A PATTERN, not a list. These directories hold key material — the pepper, the
# session key and the license signing key — and every new tool that takes a
# `--data-dir` invents another one: data-e2e/ and data-e2e-full/ for §8, then
# data-loadgen/ for the load harness, which enumerating had already missed.
# Committing a signing key because a directory was named something new is not a
# mistake worth leaving available.
data/
data-*/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ...with one carve-out. `data/` above is unanchored on purpose — it has to be, or
# the next tool to invent `data-whatever/` slips through. The cost is that it also
# matches any directory named `data` at any depth, and docs-site/ has one holding
# the site's typed event and board tables. That is source, not runtime state, and
# it is re-included by naming the directory itself (git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is still excluded).
!docs-site/src/data/

# --- deployment (docs/operations.md) ---
#
# deploy.env holds every secret the deployment needs — the IdP client secrets,
# the Cloudflare API token, the VM's address and its host key. It is the ONLY
# place they exist outside the VM, and it must never become the second.
infra/deploy.env
# What `make release` shipped, by image ID. Machine-written, per-machine.
infra/.release.env
# Diagnostics bundles and fetched backups. The bundles carry no secrets by
# design, but a fetched backup carries player data.
diagnostics/

# --- scratch ---
contracts/testdata/tmp/
site/e2e/.report/
site/e2e/.results/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store

node_modules/docs-site/dist/
docs-site/node_modules/
docs-site/.astro/
